# Milestone 2 Phase B — application orchestration, fixtures and fake printer source
#
# Board: Waveshare ESP32-S3-LCD-2.8 (non-touch, SKU 30223)
# Profile: hardware-validation · ESP-IDF v5.5.4
# Date: 2026-08-05
#
# This is the FINAL re-validation, run against the code as it stands after the
# pre-commit review moved the scenario sweep policy out of the validation flow and
# into FakeSource::sweep(). An earlier run against the pre-refactor code produced the
# same figures; the two are compared in the record.
#
# Two runs are recorded, in order:
#
#   A. Unattended run. Built from the hardware-validation profile with
#      PRD_UI_VALIDATION_SCENE and PRD_DISPLAY_TEST_PATTERNS turned off, so the
#      fixture and scenario log is not interleaved with the LVGL render soak's
#      per-transfer ESP_EARLY_LOGV output. That output is compile-time only, cannot
#      be filtered at run time, and corrupts individual log lines rather than merely
#      diluting them. Everything else about the profile is unchanged.
#
#   B. Button-control run, same image. Four physical BOOT presses: short, long, long,
#      very long — exercising step, pause, resume and restart, with the pause landing
#      at a scenario boundary, which is where the Phase B pause defect lived.
#
# Filtered to the prd.* tags. Full unfiltered captures are not committed: the combined
# size across the session exceeds 4 MB, almost all ESP-IDF verbose driver output.
#
# ===========================================================================
# RUN A — cold boot, 21-fixture catalogue, nine-scenario sweep through
#         FakeSource::sweep(), catalogue wrap with rising generations
# ===========================================================================
